From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:36:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: end an input's buffering once a queue is full by
 time

An input with no cache status left its buffering wait only when a
queue no longer accepted data. The queue counts that by data size, so
a slow source can take minutes to fill it and a short item never
does, and the picture stayed frozen meanwhile.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -0,8 +0,12 @@
     }
     else
     {
+      // a queue full by time also ends the wait: AcceptsData counts data, which a slow source can
+      // take minutes to fill and a short item never fills
       if ((!m_VideoPlayerAudio->AcceptsData() && m_CurrentAudio.id >= 0) ||
-          (!m_VideoPlayerVideo->AcceptsData() && m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0))
+          (!m_VideoPlayerVideo->AcceptsData() && m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0) ||
+          (m_VideoPlayerAudio->GetLevel() >= 100 && m_CurrentAudio.id >= 0) ||
+          (m_processInfo->GetLevelVQ() >= 100 && m_CurrentVideo.id >= 0))
         SetCaching(CACHESTATE_INIT);
     }
 
